  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The proposed single storey front extension, by reason of its unacceptable and inappropriate design, positioning and excessive scale, would appear as an incongruous and visually obtrusive addition within the street scene that would fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the host dwelling, the Pinner Hill Estate Conservation Area and the Special Character Area. The applicant has failed to demonstrate any clear and convincing justification for this harm, nor would the proposal deliver public benefits sufficient to outweigh the identified heritage harm. The proposal is therefore contrary to the relevant development plan policies and the heritage conservation objectives of the National Planning Policy Framework, in particular the requirement for clear and convincing justification for heritage harm and the balancing of such harm against public benefits. As such, the development would have a detrimental impact contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 and HC1 of The London Plan (2021), Policies GR1 and HE1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021 - 2041), the adopted Supplementary Planning Document Residential Design Guide (2010) and the Pinner Hill Conservation Area Management Strategy (2009).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
